    "result_text": "The full build passes (green). \n\n## Summary\n\nThe `membershipTier` rule is a derived field on the owner read model, so I added it alongside the existing derived fields (`displayName`, `membershipNumber`, `householdId`) rather than growing any handler function.\n\nTwo files touched:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field/setter that serializes to `$.membershipTier`.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping(target = \"membershipTier\", expression = \"java(membershipTier(owner))\")` line to `toOwnerDto`, plus a new small, self-contained `membershipTier(owner)` default method (CC low, no dependency on the rest of the class):\n\n```java\ndefault String membershipTier(Owner owner) {\n    boolean unique = Integer.valueOf(0).equals(owner.getNamesakeCount());\n    boolean hasEmail = owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank();\n    return unique && hasEmail ? \"SILVER\" : \"BRONZE\";\n}\n```\n\nThis keeps structural impact low: the only edited method (`toOwnerDto`) is a one-line annotation change with CC 1, and the new logic lives in a cohesive helper with no surrounding complexity. Both new acceptance tests (`coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail`, `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail`) and the full suite pass.",
